verdicts.corrected_claim:
lgpio 0.2.2.0 (2024-03-29) is still the newest version on PyPI. Its metadata has no requires_python. Wheels exist only for cp39–cp312, as linux_armv7l, manylinux_2_34_aarch64 and manylinux_2_34_x86_64. There are no musllinux wheels, and the manylinux wheels need glibc >= 2.34.
On Python 3.13+, pip builds from the sdist, which needs:
- swig, because lgpio.i is compiled;
- a C compiler (gcc / build-essential);
- Python headers: Debian's python3-dev for the system interpreter (native venv on trixie). Official python:3.13* images already include their own headers under /usr/local/include, so installing python3-dev there is unnecessary;
- either the system liblgpio (the default branch of setup.py links -llgpio) or env PYPI=1, which statically compiles the bundled src/lg*.c and rgpiod.c. These sources are included in the 0.2.2.0 sdist.
